meta {
  name: tag: xyops (config-file)
  type: http
  seq: 26
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/pods/templates/xyops/tags
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  X-Tapis-Token: {{X-Tapis-Token}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "kind": "pod",
    "pod_definition": {
      "image": "pixlcore/xyops:latest",
      "description": "xyOps configured by a MOUNTED config.json (pixl-server conf/config.json) instead of XYOPS_<key> env overrides. secret_key interpolated from the pod secret_map so encrypted data survives restarts.",
      "time_to_stop_default": -1,
      "secret_map": { "XYOPS_SECRET_KEY": "${pods:random:32}" },
      "volume_mounts": {
        "/opt/xyops/conf/config.json": {
          "type": "ephemeral",
          "config_content": "{\"base_app_url\":\"http://localhost:5522\",\"email_from\":\"xyops@localhost\",\"secret_key\":\"${pods:secrets:XYOPS_SECRET_KEY}\",\"log_dir\":\"/opt/xyops/logs\",\"log_filename\":\"xyops.log\",\"debug_level\":5,\"maintenance\":\"04:00\",\"job_data_expire_days\":180,\"WebServer\":{\"http_port\":5522,\"http_htdocs_dir\":\"/opt/xyops/htdocs\",\"http_max_upload_size\":104857600,\"http_static_ttl\":3600,\"https\":0},\"Storage\":{\"engine\":\"Filesystem\",\"Filesystem\":{\"base_dir\":\"/opt/xyops/data\"}}}",
          "config_permissions": "0644",
          "config_update_mode": "always"
        },
        "/opt/xyops/data": { "type": "ephemeral", "read_only": false }
      },
      "networking": {
        "default": { "protocol": "http", "port": 5522, "tapis_auth": true, "tapis_auth_allowed_users": ["*"], "tapis_auth_return_path": "/" }
      },
      "healthchecks": {
        "readiness": { "http_get_path": "/", "http_get_port": 5522, "initial_delay_seconds": 15, "period_seconds": 10 },
        "liveness": { "http_get_path": "/", "http_get_port": 5522, "initial_delay_seconds": 45, "period_seconds": 15 },
        "networking_requires_ready": true
      },
      "resources": { "cpu_request": 500, "cpu_limit": 2000, "mem_request": 512, "mem_limit": 2048 }
    },
    "tag": "config-file",
    "commit_message": "xyOps via mounted pixl-server config.json (ephemeral config_content) instead of env overrides - demonstrates file-based config.",
    "description": "xyOps configured entirely by a mounted conf/config.json rather than XYOPS_<key> env vars."
  }
}

docs {
  ## xyOps configured BY FILE - `config-file`

  Answer to "can xyOps be configured by file?": **yes.** xyOps runs on PixlCore's `pixl-server`
  framework (same as Cronicle), which loads settings from `conf/config.json`. The `XYOPS_<Key>`
  env vars used by the `stats` / `tapis-workflow` tags are actually **overrides layered on top of
  that file** - so you can mount a full config.json and drop the env overrides, which this tag does.

  ### How it works here
  - `conf/config.json` is injected as an **ephemeral mount** (`config_content`), the same mechanism
    the gatus stacks use for `config.yaml`.
  - `secret_key` in the file is `${pods:secrets:XYOPS_SECRET_KEY}` - `interpolate_config_content`
    fills it from the pod `secret_map` at start, so encrypted storage survives restarts.
  - Env overrides still WIN over the file if you also set `XYOPS_<key>` - handy for one-off tweaks.

  ### VERIFY the path + schema before relying on this
  Not verifiable locally (no published image; build-from-repo only). Confirm two things from the
  xyOps repo (github.com/pixlcore/xyops):
  1. **Config path** - pixl-server reads `conf/config.json` under the app root; confirm the image's
     app root is `/opt/xyops` so the mount path is right (check the Dockerfile WORKDIR).
  2. **Key names** - the block mirrors Cronicle (WebServer.http_port, Storage, secret_key,
     base_app_url, log_dir). Diff it against the repo's `sample_conf/config.json`.

  ### Still declarative-limited
  Monitors/workflows live in the SQLite store under `/opt/xyops/data` (made in the UI/API) - the
  config.json configures the SERVER, not the monitors. `/opt/xyops/data` is ephemeral here; add a
  tapisvolume for durable history.
}
